# Template for .env.local (gitignored). Copy it, then `docker compose up -d` to apply changes.
#
# .env.local is read twice:
#   1. by Docker Compose (env_file in compose.yaml) -> becomes real environment of the app container,
#      which is what Xdebug needs because it reads XDEBUG_MODE at PHP startup;
#   2. by Symfony's Dotenv inside the container -> overrides values from .env / .env.<env>.
#
# Real credentials (Twilio, SMTP) belong here and never in a committed file.

# debug | off | coverage | develop. Breakpoints fire only for requests carrying ?XDEBUG_TRIGGER=1
# (HTTP) or -e XDEBUG_TRIGGER=1 (CLI, see `make test-debug`) because start_with_request=trigger.
XDEBUG_MODE=debug
